"Wrote the merge plan to /Users/liammagnier/Developer/project/juno/docs/design/artifacts-design/04-MERGE-PLAN.md (about 210 KB, 16 sections and 2 appendices). I edited no product code and made no commits.\n1. **Structure.** The risk-first dated release train (W1 = 2026-09-28) is the spine. Inside it sit the Claude-faithful product order (data, then surface, then the AI loop, then Docs and Decks, with the Design door last) and the object-first view and Mac design. \u00a70 has a 20-row table that settles each point the proposals disagreed on and says why.\n2. **Dates.** The losses stop in R1\u2013R2 (by 2026-10-08). First light for the owner cohort is 2026-11-26. Day one is 2027-01-21 for the owner and 2027-02-11 for everyone, gated on the find rate. Launch (Docs, Decks, Play, Design row removed) is 2027-04-01. Contraction follows once the compatibility window closes.\n3. **Object model.** Artifacts are account-owned. Each has a working copy (the head), immutable sealed versions, publishing pinned to a version, a 30-day trash, and a deletion ledger that records the reason for every hard delete in Postgres. There is a mermaid ER diagram and a type registry table covering 12 types plus capabilities.\n4. **New kinds.** `DOC` and `DECK` (later `DESIGN_SYSTEM`) are real enum values, created only for accounts whose every recent device can read them. Old builds see them as tombstones and cannot write to them. This replaces risk-first's \"profiles\" and Claude-faithful's down-conversion.\n5. **Anchor.** One hidden `kind: \"anchor\"` conversation per account, instead of one per deleted chat. It never holds messages or becomes a chat; the first Ask moves that one artifact into a new chat. This answers the conversion-contract, flip-rule and asset must-fixes. It breaks the \"no new `Conversation.kind`\" rule in TWO_PRODUCTS \u00a75, so D13 asks the owner to accept that until contraction.\n6. **Sync trigger.** The change-capture trigger rewrite ships in Phase 1 (R5) with a staging parity test. I re-read the migration SQL and confirmed the triggers resolve the owner through Conversation today.\n7. **Installed Mac and iPhone builds.** Four protections, with an exact rule for what old builds are sent (tombstones, never silent omission). An oversized-version filter ships in R4 because X-09 is live today. A field-preserving save fixes X-14 for Mac 1.6.0 with no native release.\n8. **The view.** The panel runs the editor's compact layout. The full window is the stage plus one leading tabbed pane (composer pinned) plus one trailing pane, with the same layout at `/a/{id}` from every entry point. The card has one Open. The send button stays send/stop; steering goes through the placeholder.\n9. **Wireframes and diagrams.** 7 ASCII wireframes: panel, full window, Artifacts home with New, card states, Share/Publish, Mac on the glass shell, iPhone. Mermaid diagrams for the object model and a dated gantt.\n10. **Motion.** A table covering web, reduced motion, Mac and iPhone, in Juno tokens. `spring.layout` for panel to full window; the transcript fades rather than re-wrapping; the composer travels as one view. One new token, `--delay-reveal`.\n11. **AI loop.** A re-emit guard in R1 contains X-05 and X-06. The full loop (persisted proposals, compare-and-swap, \"your edit wins\") rolls out per kind, gated by a golden eval set built in Phase 1. Stored messages are never rewritten; old artifact bodies are left out when building the model's context instead.\n12. **X-01.** Split: owner-only previews on a separate domain in W2, scripted public pages only once governance (G1) is live in R4. The Make choice is a mark at the start of the composer field (PREMIUM_AUDIT \u00a72d superseded FLAT_UI \u00a74's pill beside `+`).\n13. **Mac and iPhone.** Asks the glass session, via the owner, to drop its Design row before release. Document windows use plain panes; Grid/List goes in the View menu, not \u23181/\u23182. N1, N2 and N3 are cut from `main`. iPhone design editing is read-only from W4 and field edits return in N2 (W17).\n14. **Roadmap.** Phases 0A\u20138 each have exit criteria, X-ids, R-ids, flags and rollback. Also: a flag registry, 20 \"must not ship before\" rules, a stated capacity (three parallel lanes) with a cut list, and 26 owner decisions with recommended answers.\n15. **Traceability.** \"What we will not copy\" and a Claude/Figma comparison table are included. Appendix A maps every judge must-fix to the section that answers it. Appendix B lists X-01\u2026X-33 and R-001\u2026R-101 by phase; a script confirmed full coverage."